{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "_comment": [
    "This file is a template for .claude/settings.local.json.",
    "Customize it to match project-config.md and place it as",
    ".claude/settings.local.json.",
    "",
    "What to customize:",
    "- Build tool: npm (default) / yarn / pnpm / bun",
    "  → see _comment_pkg_manager and swap the matching lines in allow",
    "- Quality tools: biome (default) / eslint + prettier",
    "  → see _comment_quality_tools and swap the matching lines in allow",
    "- Test runner: vitest (default) / jest",
    "- MCP: adjust to the MCP plugins you actually use",
    "",
    "Safety mechanisms (defense in depth):",
    "- Layer 0: sandbox (off by default; see _comment_sandbox to opt in)",
    "- Layer 1: hooks (defined in settings.json; active even with --dangerously-skip-permissions)",
    "    PreToolUse(Bash/Edit|Write|NotebookEdit/Skill) + PostToolUse + PostToolUseFailure",
    "    + UserPromptSubmit + SessionStart/SessionEnd + SubagentStart/SubagentStop",
    "    + PreCompact/PostCompact + Stop(verify-gate verification gate / notify) / Notification + PermissionDenied(denial log) + TaskCompleted(verification gate)",
    "- Layer 2: deny / ask rules (already in settings.json; do not override them here)",
    "- Layer 3: allow rules (this file, active in normal mode)",
    "- meta : self-SAST via scan-harness.sh (constitution hash / secret leakage / deny weakening)",
    "",
    "Evaluation order is deny > ask > allow. An operation listed under ask in",
    "settings.json still prompts even if you allow it here (that is intentional)."
  ],
  "_comment_file_rules": [
    "Important: only Edit(path) and Read(path) are consulted for file permissions.",
    "Write(path) / NotebookEdit(path) / Glob(path) / MultiEdit(path) are accepted but",
    "never consulted, and produce a startup warning. Use Edit(path) even when what",
    "you want to permit is a Write."
  ],
  "_comment_auto_mode": [
    "Relation to auto mode (the default permission mode on Pro / Max / Team):",
    "- deny rules in settings.json apply before the classifier; ask rules always prompt, even in auto mode",
    "- `permissions.defaultMode: \"auto\"` and `autoMode.*` are NOT read from project / local settings (official spec).",
    "  Put them in your personal ~/.claude/settings.json or managed settings; /auto-mode-setup drafts them",
    "- The classifier also reads CLAUDE.md, so project-specific prohibitions belong in CLAUDE.md too",
    "- Classifier denials are logged by permission-denied-log.sh under testreport/denials/. Add repeatedly",
    "  denied legitimate actions to the allow list in this file"
  ],
  "_comment_stop_gate": [
    "Choosing a verification gate (Stop hook):",
    "- Default: verify-gate.sh (deterministic). standard = warning / strict = sent back once when no verification ran after edits",
    "- To keep working toward a condition within one conversation: /goal <condition> (model-judged every turn, session-scoped)",
    "- For a permanent model-judged gate, add a prompt-type Stop hook to this file:",
    "  \"hooks\": { \"Stop\": [ { \"hooks\": [ { \"type\": \"prompt\",",
    "    \"prompt\": \"Evaluate if Claude should stop: $ARGUMENTS. Block only if tests were not run after code changes.\" } ] } ] }",
    "  NOTE: Claude Code overrides the hook after 8 consecutive blocks. Check stop_hook_active and block only once"
  ],
  "_comment_telemetry": [
    "Observability / cost (organization rollout): to aggregate usage with OpenTelemetry, add to env:",
    "  CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY=1 / OTEL_METRICS_EXPORTER=otlp / OTEL_LOGS_EXPORTER=otlp /",
    "  OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=grpc / OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://<collector>:4317 /",
    "  OTEL_LOG_TOOL_DETAILS=1 (records skill names verbatim so unused skills can be identified)",
    "To make /usage match contracted rates, use modelPricing in managed settings.",
    "See .claude/managed-settings.example.json for an org-wide example (deny / sandbox / OTel / requiredMinimumVersion)."
  ],
  "env": {
    "CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS": "1",
    "BLUEPRINT_HOOK_PROFILE": "standard"
  },
  "_comment_hook_profile": [
    "BLUEPRINT_HOOK_PROFILE: behavior switch for the extended hooks",
    "  Honored by: user-prompt-submit / session-end / scan-harness / post-compact-restore / subagent-audit",
    "  - 'minimal':  pass-through (skip inspection). For CI / automation",
    "  - 'standard': warn only on detection (non-blocking, default)",
    "  - 'strict':   block the skill / prompt on detection. For high-risk work"
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Read(**/*)",
      "Edit(**/*.{css,js,jsx,ts,tsx,json,md,yml,yaml})",
      "Bash(npm run *)",
      "Bash(npm install *)",
      "Bash(npm uninstall *)",
      "Bash(npm view *)",
      "Bash(npm ls *)",
      "Bash(npx vitest *)",
      "Bash(npx tsc *)",
      "Bash(npx biome *)",
      "Bash(npx playwright *)",
      "Bash(npx depcruise *)",
      "Bash(npx lint-staged *)",
      "Bash(npx husky *)",
      "Bash(git status *)",
      "Bash(git diff *)",
      "Bash(git log *)",
      "Bash(git add *)",
      "Bash(git commit *)",
      "Bash(git pull *)",
      "Bash(git fetch *)",
      "Bash(git branch *)",
      "Bash(git checkout *)",
      "Bash(git merge *)",
      "Bash(git stash *)",
      "Bash(git mv *)",
      "Bash(git reset *)",
      "Bash(git restore *)",
      "Bash(git remote *)",
      "Bash(gh pr view *)",
      "Bash(gh pr list *)",
      "Bash(gh pr diff *)",
      "Bash(gh pr create *)",
      "Bash(gh repo view *)",
      "Bash(node *)",
      "Bash(ls *)",
      "WebSearch",
      "WebFetch(domain:docs.claude.com)",
      "WebFetch(domain:github.com)",
      "mcp__context7__resolve-library-id",
      "mcp__context7__query-docs",
      "mcp__plugin_context7_context7__resolve-library-id",
      "mcp__plugin_context7_context7__query-docs",
      "mcp__playwright__*",
      "mcp__plugin_playwright_playwright__*"
    ]
  },
  "_comment_allow_notes": [
    "git push / gh pr merge / gh release are listed under ask in settings.json, so",
    "they still prompt even if allowed here. Outbound operations confirm every time.",
    "",
    "WebFetch is allowed per domain. To allow everything, replace those entries with",
    "'WebFetch(domain:*)' — but note that this permits reaching any URL."
  ],
  "_comment_pkg_manager": [
    "Switching package manager — swap the npm/npx block inside allow",
    "",
    "yarn: Bash(yarn *), Bash(yarn run *), Bash(yarn add *), Bash(yarn remove *)",
    "pnpm: Bash(pnpm run *), Bash(pnpm add *), Bash(pnpm remove *), Bash(pnpm dlx *)",
    "bun:  Bash(bun run *), Bash(bun add *), Bash(bun remove *), Bash(bunx *)"
  ],
  "_comment_quality_tools": [
    "Switching quality tools — swap the npx biome line inside allow",
    "",
    "eslint + prettier: Bash(npx eslint *), Bash(npx prettier *)",
    "jest (instead of vitest): Bash(npx jest *)"
  ],
  "_comment_sandbox": [
    "Layer 0: OS sandbox. Runs Bash in isolation and restricts file and network",
    "access at the OS level, even for arbitrary subprocesses.",
    "It closes the gap that Read/Edit deny rules cannot cover — reads and writes",
    "performed by a Python or Node script.",
    "",
    "To enable, paste this block at the top level:",
    "  \"sandbox\": {",
    "    \"enabled\": true,",
    "    \"network\": { \"allowedDomains\": [\"registry.npmjs.org\", \"github.com\"] }",
    "  }",
    "",
    "Exempt individual commands that fail inside the sandbox with sandbox.excludedCommands."
  ],
  "_comment_teammate": [
    "teammateMode controls WHERE agent-team teammates are displayed.",
    "  - 'in-process': inside your main terminal pane (default)",
    "  - 'auto'      : split panes when tmux / iTerm2 are available, otherwise in-process",
    "  - 'tmux'      : split panes via tmux / iTerm2",
    "  - 'iterm2'    : native iTerm2 split panes",
    "Note: 'worktree' is NOT a teammateMode value. To isolate the repository, set",
    "      isolation: worktree in a subagent's frontmatter, or configure worktree.*.",
    "",
    "worktree.baseRef: which ref new worktrees branch from",
    "  - 'fresh' (default): branch from origin/<default-branch> (clean, matches the remote)",
    "  - 'head'           : branch from the current local HEAD (includes unpushed commits)"
  ],
  "enableAllProjectMcpServers": true,
  "teammateMode": "in-process",
  "worktree": {
    "baseRef": "head"
  }
}
